  "body": "Stacked on #1717 (base `issue/1648-wcs-page-work-offset`). Retarget this PR to `main` before #1717 merges.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\nPart 1 of issue 1649 (\"Split in two\"): the WCS page can store a flipped axis. This PR does not change posted G-code.\r\n\r\n- **Stored flags.** A new component `schema::WcsFlip([bool; 3])` is on the setup's WCS entity. \"No flip\" is stored as no component.\r\n- **One undoable command.** `SetWcsFlip::for_setup` sets the flags of a setup's WCS. It refuses an unknown setup by name. If the WCS was never placed, it places it at the identity, and undo removes it again.\r\n- **WCS page.** Three toggles, \"Flip X\", \"Flip Y\" and \"Flip Z\", are under the quarter turns. A lit toggle is a flipped axis. When an axis is flipped, a note tells the user that posting and generating are refused until the flip is cleared.\r\n- **Viewport triad.** A flipped axis is drawn in the opposite direction. A flipped WCS at the origin does not hide the world axes.\r\n- **Refusal by name.** The post verification gate and the generation door (`collect_job`) refuse a flipped WCS. An example message: \"the WCS (G54) has its X axis flipped; posting or generating with a flipped WCS is not available yet - clear the flip on the WCS page (operations: Face1)\". All post paths use the gate, so no path posts with a flip set.\r\n- **Project file v62.** A WCS row can have the optional key `flip` (`{\"x\": true}`), and only flipped axes are written. A file without the key opens with no flip. A `flip` key on a row that is not a WCS is refused as corrupt.\r\n- **Undo keeps the flip.** `DeleteEntity`, `DeleteSetup` and the datum transfer of `CreateSetup` keep the flip.\r\n- **MCP.** A new tool, `set_wcs_flip {x?, y?, z?, setup?}`. An axis that is not given keeps its flag. `get_job` shows `setups[].wcs.flip`. The camcraft-mcp skill has the tool row and a \"Shipped\" line.\r\n- **Decisions.** `docs/decisions/1720-wcs-flip-flags.md`.\r\n\r\n## How tested\r\n\r\n- `crates/app/tests/wcs_flip.rs` (new, 10 tests). It pins these points:\r\n  - the command, undo and redo;\r\n  - the refusal of an unknown setup;\r\n  - the post refusal by name, and the same stream after the flip is cleared;\r\n  - the generation refusal by name;\r\n  - the setup name in the message;\r\n  - DeleteSetup and DeleteEntity undo;\r\n  - the datum transfer;\r\n  - the project round trip, an old file, and a corrupt row;\r\n  - the MCP tool and `get_job`.\r\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/wcs_flip_tests.rs` (new, 3 tests). It pins the toggle layout and live state, the click to the command, the reversed triad, undo and redo, and the status line.\r\n- The existing suites `wcs_page_tests`, `wcs_gizmo_tests` and `wcs_circle_tests` pass.\r\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/1648-wcs-page-work-offset`: the app step (302 suites) passed in 1279 s. A file that I wrote into the worktree during the run made the gate VOID before its ui step. Then I ran the same ui step command by hand on the same tree, and it passed (lib 778 tests and 12 suites).\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- No before/after screenshots: this worker cannot start the GUI. The maintainer must add them before `/merge-ready` offers the PR.\r\n- Posting with a flip (part 2 of issue 1649) is not in this PR. There are no NC golden changes.\r\n- No script verb. The decision file gives the reason.\r\n\r\nChangelog: The WCS page can store a flipped X, Y or Z axis (Flip X / Flip Y / Flip Z, MCP `set_wcs_flip`); a setup with a flipped axis is refused by name at post and generation until part 2 carries the flip into the program; project files are now v62.\r\n\r\nEffort: high\r\n\r\nProcess change: yes\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\nFixes #1720\r\n",
